id: pm-gh1576
title: "GH-1576: guard SDK and CLI mutations with expected item revisions"
description: Reported read-decide-write races in extension consumers need an optional atomic expected-item-hash precondition checked at the mutation commit boundary. Preserve existing no-precondition behavior and distinguish this from mutation lease fencing.
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: concurrency,"gh:1576",sdk
created_at: "2026-10-24T16:12:40.963Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-02T14:29:14.974Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-02T14:26:27.656Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-02T14:26:27.656Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "Define a public optional expected revision/hash contract across single-item and bulk SDK/CLI/MCP mutations; Check each precondition under the authoritative item lock at commit time and refuse stale writes without acknowledged item or history changes; Return typed current revision and bounded actionable change evidence; Deterministic concurrent controls cover closeout tags, collection cleanup, claim and bulk partial outcomes without weakening lease fencing."
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "A revision scope (AsyncLocalStorage) is evaluated in the locked item store after the item lock is taken and before any write, and advances past the scope's own commits. It covers every mutateItem caller, delete, restore, bulk rows and extension SDK writes. Public SDK readItemRevision/withExpectedItemRevisions with a checked/unchecked receipt. Global --expect-hash (bare hash binds <id>, <id>=<hash> names targets). expectHash on 19 MCP/runAction item-writing actions. The refusal carries expected/current revision plus details.changes_since (10 newest history entries with fields). stdin-json accepts item_hash. GH-1620: transaction docs state the lock serializes coordinators only, and a negative-control spec proves the guard turns the lost update into a refusal."
expected_result: A write based on a stale observed revision refuses atomically and supplies bounded recovery evidence
actual_result: "Verified: a stale close/update/comment/files/restore/delete refuses with exit 4 and writes nothing. The fresh revision is admitted, and a multi-write claim+update advances. An interleaved unscoped peer write refuses the next step. update-many fails only the stale row. MCP handleRequest refuses a stale pm_update. 100/100/100/100 coverage and the full quality:static chain pass."
